# motifmatchr 1.36.1

Bug fix: background correction of log-odds PWMs used the wrong sign, so
scores were computed as log(p * bg_new / bg_old^2) instead of
log(p / bg_new). Matches and scores change whenever the scanning background
(e.g. the default bg = "subject") differs from the PWM's stored background.
Results with bg = "even" and uniform-background PWMs are unchanged
(GreenleafLab/motifmatchr#13; reported by Juliane Rohland).

Bug fix: PWMatrix inputs containing frequencies (e.g. toPWM(type = "prob"))
are now converted to log2 odds against the background; previously raw
frequencies were used as scores. PWMs with zero probabilities or non-finite
scores now give an informative error instead of crashing.

Build fix: the package now compiles with RcppArmadillo >= 15. The C++11
requirement was removed and R's default C++ standard is used
(GreenleafLab/motifmatchr#12; contributed by I-Hsuan Lin). motifmatchr now
requires R >= 4.3.

pwmType() now tolerates small rounding errors when detecting log-odds PWMs,
so motif collections with imprecise column sums no longer fail
(GreenleafLab/motifmatchr#9; contributed by Pierre-Luc Germain).

# motifmatchr 0.99.7

API changed from snake_case to camelCase. snake_case versions of methods
kept with deprecation notice.

# motifmatchr 0.99.6

Genome no longer defaults to hg19 when subject is GenomicRanges or
RangedSummarizedExperiment, but tries to pull assoicated genome build from
object. Genome can be provided as BSgenome, FaFile, DNAStringSet object, or
short string (e.g. "hg19").

Added BSgenomeViews method.



